ALL = ' And all that is required to complete the work fully ready for operation in accordance with the drawings and specifications, even if not expressly stated.'
T = {
'LS-19': ('Distribution Boards and Main Feeders', 'Supply and installation of sub‑distribution boards to IEC 61439 (ABB or Schneider), breakers and main cables (Riyadh Cables) from the source to the boards, and modification of existing boards, based on a load study, phase balancing, voltage drop not exceeding 3% and 20% spare capacity, with labelling, directories, insulation tests, thermographic inspection and handover as per drawings.'),
'LS-20': ('Low Current Systems', 'Supply, installation and cabling of low current systems: Cat6A data and telephone network, wireless access points, nurse call, IP CCTV, sound and public address, and access control, including outlets, cables, containment segregated from power, cabinets, panels and independent earthing, with certification testing of every point, labelling and handover with as‑built drawings, as per drawings.'),
'LS-21': ('Fire Alarm System', 'Supply and installation, or modification and extension, of the addressable fire alarm system within the scope: detectors, manual call points, audible and visual alarm devices, monitor and control modules and short‑circuit isolators, with LSZH fire‑resistant cables, interfaced with the main panel, HVAC, doors and other systems, with programming, full testing, handover and Civil Defense approval.'),
'LS-22': ('HVAC and Ventilation Works', 'Removal and replacement / redistribution of HVAC and ventilation works within the scope: units, ductwork, insulation, supply and return grilles, dampers and controls, and connection to the existing system, including testing, balancing and commissioning as per drawings.'),
'LS-23': ('Plumbing and Drainage Works', 'Removal and replacement, or execution, of hot and cold water supply (PPR thermal pipes; buried HDPE), drainage and vent piping (UPVC Class 4), sanitary ware, mixers, valves and accessories as per drawings, including pressure testing and connection to existing networks.'),
'LS-24': ('Fire Fighting System', 'Modification and extension of the water fire fighting system within the scope (sprinklers, hose cabinets, extinguishers) as per drawings and Civil Defense requirements, including supports, testing and handover.'),
'LS-25': ('Medical Gases', 'Installation of medical gas outlets (oxygen, medical air, vacuum) with copper piping, isolation valves and alarm panels within the scope as per drawings and specifications, with testing and certification.'),
'LS-26': ('Water Heaters, Pumps and Tanks', 'Supply and installation / replacement of water heaters, circulation and booster pumps (duty and standby sets with variable speed control and pressure vessel), water tanks and their accessories and control panels as per drawings and approved capacity calculations, including bases, connections, insulation, testing and commissioning.'),
'LS-27': ('Site Works and Pavements', 'Rehabilitation of external pavements, walkways and entrances (interlock / concrete / granite as per drawings), including excavation, levelling, sub‑base layers, kerbs and surface drainage.'),
'LS-28': ('Canopies, Ramps and Accessible Routes', 'Supply and construction of entrance canopies, ramps, handrails and accessible routes as per drawings and the Saudi Building Code requirements for universal access.'),
'LS-29': ('Landscaping and Irrigation', 'Execution of planting, green areas and an automatic irrigation network (HDPE or 10‑bar UPVC pipes, solenoid valves, central controller, sprinklers and drippers) within the scope as per drawings, with salt‑ and heat‑tolerant plants and tested, salt‑free agricultural soil, including maintenance and watering until provisional acceptance.'),
'LS-30': ('External Lighting', 'Supply and installation of external lighting poles and LED fittings with protection of not less than IP66, façade and entrance lighting, cabling and control by photocell or timer as per drawings, with removal of the existing and testing.'),
'LS-35': ('Inpatient Room Upgrade — Single (One Bed)', 'Complete upgrade of a single‑bed inpatient room, including: removal of existing finishes and installations, floors (medical vinyl / porcelain) and skirting, ceilings, hygienic paints, bedhead unit (headwall) with medical gas, power, lighting and nurse call outlets, the door and its hardware, electrical installations and lighting (general, examination, night), HVAC and ventilation, complete refurbishment of the en‑suite toilet to accessibility requirements, low current (nurse call, TV, network), fire alarm, windows and curtains, non‑medical furniture, and cleaning and handover — as per drawings and specifications. Price per room.'),
'LS-36': ('Inpatient Room Upgrade — Double (Two Beds)', 'Complete upgrade of a two‑bed inpatient room, including: removal of existing finishes and installations, floors and skirting, ceilings, hygienic paints, two bedhead units (headwalls) with medical gas, power, lighting and nurse call outlets for each bed, a privacy curtain between the beds with its ceiling track, the door and its hardware, electrical installations and lighting, HVAC and ventilation, complete refurbishment of the en‑suite toilet, low current (nurse call, TV, network), fire alarm, windows and curtains, non‑medical furniture, and cleaning and handover — as per drawings and specifications. Price per room.'),
'LS-37': ('Inpatient Room Upgrade — Suite (Two Rooms Combined)', 'Combining two adjacent inpatient rooms into one by removing the dividing wall with structural strengthening of the opening as per drawings and the structural engineer’s report, and its complete upgrade to include a bed area and a seating/reception area for companions: floors and skirting, ceilings and gypsum details, paints and cladding, bedhead unit with medical gas, power and nurse call outlets, re‑routing of power, lighting, HVAC and ventilation, refurbishment or combination of the two toilets as per drawings, a pantry where required, low current and fire alarm, doors, windows and curtains, non‑medical furniture, and cleaning and handover. Price per suite.'),
'LS-38': ('Inpatient Suite Upgrade — Royal (Full Suite)', 'Complete upgrade of a royal‑class inpatient suite, including: bedroom, sitting and reception lounge, companion room, two toilets, pantry and private entrance as per drawings; with luxury finishes (floors, cladding and gypsum ceilings with concealed lighting), bedhead unit with medical gas, power and nurse call outlets, electrical installations and lighting with a lighting and curtain control system, HVAC and ventilation, complete plumbing works, low current (nurse call, screens, network, sound), fire alarm, doors, windows and curtains, non‑medical furniture and furnishings, and cleaning and handover. Price per suite.'),
'LS-39': ('Nurse Station and Common Corridors Upgrade', 'Upgrade of the nurse station, corridors and common areas of the inpatient ward: nurse station counter and fixed furniture, main nurse call panel, floors, skirting, guards and corridor handrails, ceilings and lighting, paints, medication and supplies room and linen store, corridor doors and fire doors, HVAC, low current and fire alarm in common areas, and wayfinding signage — as per drawings and specifications.'),
'LS-31': ('Testing, Commissioning and Balancing', 'Carrying out commissioning and balancing tests for all systems (electrical, HVAC, plumbing, fire fighting, low current) in the presence of the Department’s representative and the consultant, including: testing, adjusting and balancing (TAB) by a specialist company, pressure testing of pipework, insulation and earthing tests, trial operation of each system and integrated testing of fire systems, rectification of comments, submission of approved test reports and obtaining approvals of the competent authorities (Civil Defense and others).'),
'LS-32': ('Final Cleaning, Handover and Documentation', 'Comprehensive final cleaning, removal of debris and repair of any damage; handover of as‑built drawings, operation and maintenance (O&M) manuals and warranty certificates: a general warranty of not less than one year from provisional acceptance and manufacturers’ warranties for equipment for their respective periods; spare parts for critical systems as recommended by the manufacturers; and training of the operations team on electrical, mechanical and safety systems before acceptance.'),
'LS-33': ('Safety, Permits and Coordination', 'Compliance with occupational safety and health requirements (Saudi Safety Council), personal protective equipment and the emergency plan, and infection control when working inside or next to an operating facility; obtaining the necessary permits; coordination with operational departments and competent authorities throughout execution; and submission of the work plan, time schedule and periodic reports.'),
'LS-41': ('Site Preparation, Hoarding and Project Signboard', 'Cleaning and levelling of the general site and removal of vegetation, debris, stockpiles and temporary roads, preparing it for the start of work; providing a construction waste skip throughout execution and disposing of waste per municipality instructions; supply and installation of temporary hoarding around the site: the frontage on the main street 2.40 m high of plywood panels with a full‑length high‑quality printed banner per the approved design, and the remaining boundaries 1.80 m high of painted or galvanized corrugated sheeting, all on steel frames fixed with anchors or concrete bases designed for wind loads; supply and installation of the external project signboard, 5.00 m overall height and 2.50 m wide, on a steel frame with concrete bases: an upper panel 2.50×2.50 m with the project perspective and name, and four lower panels 0.50×2.50 m for the names of the donor, contractor, consultant and Al Ahsa Health Cluster, in aluminium or painted sheet steel with high‑quality printing, with designs approved before execution; and removal of the temporary hoarding and signs at handover.' + ALL),
'LS-42': ('Temporary Offices, Facilities, Power and Lighting', 'Supply and fitting out of portable site offices throughout execution, as a minimum: an office for the Contractor and an office for the project management team and consultant of not less than 3×4 m, each furnished, air‑conditioned and provided with internet and a screen of not less than 50 inches; at least two toilets equipped with washbasins and proper drainage; suitable areas for storing and protecting materials; keeping the offices and toilets clean with daily air‑conditioning and water, and providing drinking water, kettle, refrigerator and hospitality supplies; providing temporary power to the site and bearing its cost, and sufficient lighting for evening work or during Ramadan when needed; and removal of all of the above and reinstatement of the site on completion.' + ALL),
'LS-43': ('Engineering Studies, Calculations and Laboratory Tests', 'Preparation and submission of supporting engineering studies and calculations for approval before supply and execution, including: review of the soil investigation report and approval of the cement type and soil aggressiveness; structural verification of flat slabs (punching shear at columns) approved by the consultant; an electrical load study, phase balancing and voltage drop (≤ 3%) leaving 20% spare in each board; cooling load calculation at an outdoor design temperature of not less than 46 °C; pump, pipe sizing and fire fighting calculations (flow and pressure); UPS battery calculation; a lighting level study; and wind‑load design of the curtain wall by a licensed office; and carrying out laboratory tests at an accredited laboratory in the presence of the consultant, documented in records: concrete samples, compaction density of backfill and base layers (≥ 95% modified Proctor), flood test of waterproofing, pressure tests of water and fire fighting pipes, earthing, and trial operation of every system; and supplying certificates of origin and conformity (SASO) and UL/FM certificates for fire system materials.' + ALL),
'LS-44': ('Excavation, Backfilling and Grading', 'Calculation of excavation and cut quantities at the Contractor’s responsibility from the drawings and soil report, and executing them to the depths and levels required for concrete works with suitable equipment, separating suitable excavated material and disposing of the remainder to the approved municipal dump, and water spraying to prevent dust; backfilling with approved soil per the consultant’s recommendations and soil tests in layers of 20 to 40 cm with wetting and mechanical compaction to a density of not less than 95% of modified Proctor, testing each layer; and final site grading with falls achieving drainage. Note: conditions not visible before excavation (groundwater, cavities, soil improvement works) shall be addressed when encountered by a separate order at a cost borne by the Owner at the prevailing market rate.' + ALL),
'LS-45': ('Termite Control', 'Supply and spraying of approved termite and insect treatment on horizontal and vertical surfaces over the entire excavation area, beneath buildings and around their perimeter at the lower levels, at the concentration and quantities recommended by the manufacturer, before pouring blinding concrete and before backfilling, with a warranty certificate from the applicator.' + ALL),
}
